{"title":"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/5/805452ee372321839953fbd750cd9b23b973a3df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/7/c67b8642935b24d120f8224fb7971f0c75098009.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QT$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/2/6627137ea2353e84e0999de14a060fb754fa315c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RU$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> intersect at a common point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, as shown. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is joined to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />, to form triangles. The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/0/9c0996bc1e09ec9bea2d24f55987bed7af39a94d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle P + \\angle Q + \\angle R + \\angle S + \\angle T + \\angle U$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"272\" height=\"18\" /> is\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/4/1b4b2b01a26f5a01cda0d069eef85bd24fe61f3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 450^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 270^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 360^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 540^{\\circ} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 720^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"517\" height=\"19\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the diagram and the fact that the sum of the interior angles of any triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />, We see:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/d/4dda13d87e64a38841e2209cf757c852d4a93494.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle POQ = 180^{\\circ} - (m \\angle P + m \\angle Q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"277\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/6/7b6b503cac5ebbf4ea8e4118758ec773a418e0d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle ROS = 180^{\\circ} - (m \\angle R + m \\angle S)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"273\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/c/5cc54000ae787823d95ede93b56128dd80972c13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle UOT = 180^{\\circ} - (m \\angle T + m \\angle U)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"275\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>We also see that angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/5/005a2a7f4c26937a68ef0365600a36309846fa24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ROS$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49e6a528c8ec7f4efa6fe05f283af877873be26c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$POU$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> are vertically opposite, making them equal to each other.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We see that angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/f/0af8bd418bbfcc17ee85fd2d959d120c3df86222.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$POQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49e6a528c8ec7f4efa6fe05f283af877873be26c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$POU$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/7/187532a5191507656397c92a45bd3fe52050d9fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$UOT$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> form a line. We then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/3/9638fa23fae1a7008cd9693673092fe62b0bf990.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle POQ + m \\angle POU + m\\angle UOT = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"320\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/0/d80492ed294eabd14477165fd3aeab6db841059b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ} - (m \\angle P + m\\angle Q) + 180^{\\circ} - (m \\angle R + m \\angle S) + 180^{\\circ} - (m \\angle T + m\\angle U) = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"641\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Re-arranging terms and adding the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />s up, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/c/f4c7eadeaa63862a857df88c0d9639934a335ebc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$540^{\\circ} - (m \\angle P + m\\angle Q + m\\angle R + m\\angle S + m\\angle T + m\\angle U) = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"498\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>We can let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be equal to the value in the parenthesis, which is the value we are trying to find.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa32776df2c52ef88dba1fa70c47ae933f8eeeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$540^{\\circ} - x = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"128\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/6/5e604db1e86f51eac25405a278ace8c5a770448b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 180^{\\circ} = 540^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"128\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/b/fcb7454654a7bd091effb8f54ae2928c00bb5636.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 360^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"118\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 22 (page does not exist)\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <